# The Conservatory on orchid or a field station: /etc/conservatory/conservatory.env
# Root-owned, mode 0600. Read by all three units through EnvironmentFile=.
# Never in the repo; the box's install script (Servers/install-orchid.sh, or
# Servers/install-station.sh on a station) copies this example into place when
# the file does not exist yet. On orchid the keys are yours to fill in; on a
# station the script asks for them.

# The one SQLite file, created and migrated by Fern. Outside the checkout
# (a deploy can never touch it), beside the photos.
CONSERVATORY_DB=/home/todd/conservatory-data/conservatory.db

# The photo tree, photos/yyyy/mm/<uuid>.jpg and their thumbnails, and the
# species reference images Fern fetches from Wikipedia, reference/<id>.jpg.
CONSERVATORY_DATA=/home/todd/conservatory-data

# Pl@ntNet API key (https://my.plantnet.org). Fern only; the web app never
# calls Pl@ntNet. Free tier: 500 identifications a day. One key, shared by the
# house and every station: the quota is one pool across the households.
PLANTNET_API_KEY=

# Vercel AI Gateway key (https://vercel.com/ai-gateway), for the care sheets
# Fern writes once per species. Optional: empty, Fern runs without them and
# the species page says so. Fern calls the model; the web app only checks
# that the key is set, to offer Rewrite. One key per box, each with its own
# spend limit in the gateway's dashboard, so a runaway on one box can never
# spend another's budget.
AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=

# The gateway's model slug for care sheets. Unset means this one.
#CONSERVATORY_LLM=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5

# The household's USDA hardiness zone, 1 to 13 with an optional a or b. Care
# sheets say what it means here; changing it has Fern rewrite every sheet.
#CONSERVATORY_ZONE=6a

# Health checks (the plant page's "Check health"), on with the gateway key
# above: Fern sends up to three of a plant's photos to a vision model when
# its owner asks, never by itself. The model slug, apart from CONSERVATORY_LLM
# so another can be tried on health checks alone. Unset means this one.
#CONSERVATORY_HEALTH_LLM=anthropic/claude-sonnet-5.5

# How many health checks the household may start in a day, by this box's own
# calendar (about 4 cents each on Sonnet 5.5). The web app reads it. Unset
# means 20.
#CONSERVATORY_HEALTH_DAILY_MAX=20

# The address every pot tag's QR code carries: a tag opens <this>/t/<plant id>.
# Printed labels last years, so this is the house name, never an IP or a dev
# address. The web app reads it; empty, no codes are drawn. Each box has a
# name of its own, or a gifted plant's tag opens another house's: the house is
# https://conservatory.lan, and a station is its front door,
# https://conservatory.toddtech.llc/<station> (#113), which follows the box
# through every change of LAN address. install-station.sh writes that value.
CONSERVATORY_URL=https://conservatory.lan

# The branch the deploy watcher follows (#113). Orchid leaves this unset and
# follows main. A station follows conservatory-station-stable, the release
# channel: main with a delay, moved to main's tip once nightly.
# install-station.sh writes this line; the checkout must sit on the same branch.
#CONSERVATORY_DEPLOY_BRANCH=conservatory-station-stable

# Not here: NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH, the path the web app is served under on a
# station (/conservatory, #113). It is a build-time value, read from
# web/.env.local (owned by todd, written by install-station.sh), because the
# build runs as todd, who cannot read this file. Orchid has no such file.
